Original commit body from cbd00f2:

Two UX issues fixed when using -x/--exclude-tests:

1. Structure section now always uses the modern tree format (├── and └──)
   even when -x excludes all source files. Previously fell back to
   deprecated bullet-list format.

2. Representativeness table now shows when -x is used, displaying
   coverage for Additional Files sections. Previously hidden when
   all source symbols were excluded.

Implementation:
- Added _format_structure_tree_toplevel() for tree format with no
  important files - shows top-level directories with item counts
- Changed stats flags (has_source_files, has_additional_files, etc.)
  to be set when sections are added, not just when in-degree available
- Updated main flow to always use _format_structure_tree(), which now
  handles empty important_files via the new helper function
